+    "---\n",
+    "# IV) Custom Regime: Overriding Physical Constants and Derivative Expressions\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The `KIonEx` model exposes **three levels of customization** that can be\n",
+    "changed on a model instance without modifying the library source code:\n",
+    "\n",
+    "1. **Model parameters** (`J`, `eta`, `Delta`, `K_bath`, …) — set at\n",
+    "   construction time or changed on the instance directly.\n",
+    "2. **`dfun_constants`** — a dictionary of physical constants\n",
+    "   (`g_Cl`, `g_Kl`, `rho`, etc.) that are baked into the generated numba\n",
+    "   code at kernel build time.\n",
+    "3. **`state_variable_dfuns`** — symbolic derivative expressions per state\n",
+    "   variable. The mako code generator reads these to produce the compiled\n",
+    "   dfun, so mutating them changes the dynamics.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "This section demonstrates a **single-node biophysical regime** with\n",
+    "customised constants and a patched $dV/dt$ expression that produces\n",
+    "**periodic spiking** driven by potassium dynamics — a qualitatively\n",
+    "different regime from the high-$K_{bath}$ bursting shown above.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "> **Key point:** all overrides must be applied *before* calling\n",
+    "> `NbBackend.build_py_func()`, because the mako template reads\n",
+    "> `dfun_constants` and `state_variable_dfuns` at code-generation time.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "> **Note on connectivity:** A single node triggers a shape bug in\n",
+    "> `_spatialize_model_parameters`, so we use 2 nodes with zero weights.\n",
+    "> Both evolve identically."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 40,
+   "id": "6299408c",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "from tvb.simulator.models.k_ion_exchange import KIonEx\n",
+    "from tvb.simulator.coupling import Linear\n",
+    "from tvb.simulator.integrators import RungeKutta4thOrderDeterministic\n",
+    "from tvb.simulator.monitors import Raw\n",
+    "from tvb.simulator.simulator import Simulator\n",
+    "from tvb.datatypes.connectivity import Connectivity"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "ffeb688c",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## 1. Create a 2-Node Zero-Weight Connectivity"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 41,
+   "id": "be8b4585",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "conn1 = Connectivity(\n",
+    "    weights=np.zeros((2, 2)),\n",
+    "    tract_lengths=np.zeros((2, 2)),\n",
+    "    region_labels=np.array(['R0', 'R1']),\n",
+    "    centres=np.zeros((2,)),\n",
+    "    speed=np.array([np.inf]),\n",
+    ")\n",
+    "conn1.configure()"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "ab84a6aa",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## 2. Override Physical Constants and Derivative Expressions\n",
+    "\n",
+    "This section customises the model at **three levels**:\n",
+    "\n",
+    "1. **`dfun_constants`** — physical constants baked into the generated numba code.\n",
+    "2. **`state_variable_dfuns['V']`** — the symbolic derivative expression for $V$.\n",
+    "   The library default omits the synaptic self-coupling term $J \\cdot r \\cdot (E - V)$;\n",
+    "   we add it here to enable the periodic-spiking regime.\n",
+    "3. **Model parameters** (`J`, `eta`, `K_bath`, …) — set in the next step.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "> **Why patch the expression?** The `state_variable_dfuns` dict is read by the\n",
+    "> mako code generator at kernel build time. Mutating it on the instance\n",
+    "> changes the generated code without modifying the library source.\n",
+    "> Sections I–III use the classic simulator path and are unaffected.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Six physical constants differ between the library defaults and the\n",
+    "calibrated biophysical regime:\n",
+    "\n",
+    "| Constant | Library default | Custom value | Description |\n",
+    "|:---------|:---------------:|:------------:|:------------|\n",
+    "| `g_Cl`   | 7.5             | **6.6**      | Chloride leak conductance |\n",
+    "| `g_Kl`   | 0.12            | **0.08**     | Potassium leak conductance |\n",
+    "| `g_Nal`  | 0.02            | **0.04**     | Sodium leak conductance |\n",
+    "| `rho`    | 250             | **320**      | Na/K pump rate |\n",
+    "| `Na_o0`  | 138             | **135**      | Baseline extracellular [Na⁺] |\n",
+    "| `Cl_i0`  | 5.0             | **5.1**      | Baseline intracellular [Cl⁻] |"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 42,
+   "id": "2284eacf",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "model_custom = KIonEx()\n",
+    "\n",
+    "# (a) Override physical constants\n",
+    "model_custom.dfun_constants.update({\n",
+    "    'g_Cl':  6.6,\n",
+    "    'g_Kl':  0.08,\n",
+    "    'g_Nal': 0.04,\n",
+    "    'rho':   320.0,\n",
+    "    'Na_o0': 135.0,\n",
+    "    'Cl_i0': 5.1,\n",
+    "})\n",
+    "\n",
+    "# (b) Patch the V derivative expression to include synaptic self-coupling J*r*(E-V).\n",
+    "# The library's default V equation omits this term; adding it is necessary\n",
+    "# for the periodic-spiking biophysical regime demonstrated here.\n",
+    "# This patch only affects the mako code generator (NbBackend), not the\n",
+    "# classic simulator path used in Sections I–III.\n",
+    "model_custom.state_variable_dfuns['V'] = (\n",
+    "    '(Vdot - R_minus*x**2 + eta + J*r*(E-V) + (R_minus/pi)*Coupling_Term*(E-V))'\n",
+    "    ' if V <= Vstar else'\n",
+    "    ' (Vdot - R_plus*x**2 + eta + J*r*(E-V) + (R_minus/pi)*Coupling_Term*(E-V))'\n",
+    ")"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "9b30d2d8",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## 3. Override Model Parameters\n",
+    "\n",
+    "These parameter values define the biophysical regime that produces\n",
+    "periodic spiking from potassium-driven instabilities."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 43,
+   "id": "26e51c9b",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "model_custom.J       = np.r_[1.0]\n",
+    "model_custom.K_bath  = np.r_[4.8]\n",
+    "model_custom.Delta   = np.r_[10.0]\n",
+    "model_custom.eta     = np.r_[10.0]\n",
+    "model_custom.tau_n   = np.r_[0.4]\n",
+    "model_custom.gamma   = np.r_[15.5]\n",
+    "model_custom.epsilon = np.r_[15.8]\n",
+    "model_custom.c_minus = np.r_[-44.24]\n",
+    "model_custom.R_minus = np.r_[0.02]\n",
+    "model_custom.c_plus  = np.r_[-20.4]\n",
